Line 2: The position of a word has to be a number, but this is text.
    let first be word "one" given to the program
                      ^^^^^

Line 3: The name of a setting has to be text, like "HOME", but this is a number.
    let home be the setting called 5
                                   ^

Line 4: Only a program result can have worked, but this is a number.
    if 5 worked, say "yes"
       ^
Run a program first, like "run "git" with "status" and call the result r", then check "if r worked:".

Line 5: The program to run has to be text, like "git", but this is a number.
    run 5 with "x".
        ^

Line 6: Each word given to a program has to be text, a number or a list of text, but this is a yes/no value.
    run "echo" with yes.
                    ^^^

Line 8: Each word given to a program has to be text, a number or a list of text, but this is a list of numbers.
    run "echo" with numbers.
                    ^^^^^^^

Line 9: The code has to be a number, but this is text.
    stop the program with code "three"
                               ^^^^^^^
